From ab8903a1a3fc14df63e3dc064054d9a8a06e27fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:49:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: do not notify vlans after the ubus context is torn
 down

hostapd_free_hapd_data() calls hostapd_ubus_free_bss() and then, three
statements later, vlan_deinit(). When that BSS holds the last ubus
reference, hostapd_ubus_ref_dec() frees the shared context and sets the
file-scope ctx to NULL. vlan_deinit() then removes each dynamic VLAN, and
every vlan_if_remove() reaches hostapd_ubus_vlan_action(), which passes
that NULL ctx to ubus_notify().

The has_subscribers guard cannot catch it: nothing clears that flag when
the object is removed, so a BSS that had a subscriber still takes the
notify path on the way down and faults.

Guard on ctx, the way hostapd_ubus_free_bss() already does.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25339
[Crescentm: from OpenWrt PR #25339 head ab8903a1a3fc14df63e3dc064054d9a8a06e27fe,
 commit ab8903a1a3; unchanged except for line numbers (applied on top of 0014)]
---
 package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c b/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
index a51560ac..ad00b58b 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
@@ -2126,6 +2126,11 @@ hostapd_ubus_vlan_action(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct hostapd_vlan *vlan,
 	void *c;
 	int i;
 
+	/* vlan_deinit() runs after hostapd_ubus_free_bss() may have dropped the
+	 * last reference and freed the shared context */
+	if (!ctx)
+		return;
+
 	if (!obj->has_subscribers)
 		return;
 
